# Prototype, reduced to what M1's parser accepts. See `bug.json` beside this
# file for why a reduced form exists at all, and for the six fields this one
# also holds to.
#
# The designed `prototype.json` (`crates/core-model/domain/workflow-samples/`)
# is already linear, already three steps, and already the one workflow
# carrying gateless steps by design — `frame` and `write_up` have no
# mechanical tier and no Judge in the designed form either. **Nothing is
# reduced here any more.** `build` was written `auto` while `human_always`
# was outside M1's carried set; it is inside it now, so the step reads as the
# designed file spells it, and a prototype stops for the person who asked for
# it before the write-up is drafted.
#
# **This workflow carries no Judge, and that is a decision rather than an
# omission.** The designed `prototype.json` carries none either. A prototype is
# built to answer a question and is thrown away; there is no criterion it
# either meets or fails, so there is nothing for a veto-only Judge to refuse.
# `docs/core-model/domain/workflows.toml` names Prototype and Documentation as
# the workflows where gateless steps are the common case, not the edge one.
#
# Adding a Judge here would spend a call per step on an answer nothing gates.
#
# **`build` declares no `evidence_scope`, and that is deliberate.** Decided by
# the owner Aug 28 2026, closing #146. It is the one runtime step that produces
# a diff with no declared footprint, and it stays that way: a prototype is built
# to answer a question and thrown away, so declaring a plan for exploratory work
# is friction with no reader. Nobody is going to measure a throwaway's diff
# against a promise it had no reason to make.
#
# Same reasoning as the Judge above. Neither a criterion nor a footprint has
# anything here to be true about.
#
# **`model: haiku` on `write_up`, and nowhere else.** `bug.json` carries the
# reasoning and the cache cost. `frame` decides what question the prototype is
# built to answer, and `build` produces the diff -- gated by nobody but read by
# the person who asked for it, which is a reason to keep it capable rather than
# a reason to make it cheap. `write_up` says what was learned once the answer is
# in, and is the one step here whose work is reporting.
{
  "version": 1,
  "workflow_id": "prototype",
  "name": "prototype",
  "structure": "linear",
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "frame",
      "label": "Frame",
      "evidence_type": "facts_note",
      "advance_gate": "auto"
    },
    {
      "id": "build",
      "label": "Build",
      "evidence_type": "diff",
      "advance_gate": "human_always"
    },
    {
      "id": "write_up",
      "label": "Write up",
      "evidence_type": "facts_note",
      "model": "haiku",
      "advance_gate": "auto"
    }
  ]
}
